  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nThe warming trend will continue through the weekend and peak \nMonday (Memorial Day) when high temps reach 85 to 93 in the \nvalleys (hottest near Grand View, ID) and 70s to mid 80s in\nthe mountains. By then flow aloft will become southwesterly and\nincrease as a deep cold upper low approaches from the Gulf of \nAlaska. A strong cold front is now forecast for Tuesday, with \nthe upper low forecast to pass directly over us on Wednesday. \nThere are similarities with Tuesday's cold front to the one \nthat occurred last week with the strong winds and blowing dust,\nso this event may become our main concern in the coming days.",
